  "headline_text": "In 2024, FARS records 39,254 road deaths. Placing each crash on the 2020 Census urban-area map, 18,760 (47.8%) died in rural areas. FARS's own rural label counts 16,005 (40.8%), which matches NHTSA's published figure. Over 2015-2024 the two labels agree on 88.42% of deaths (Cohen's kappa 0.768), but FARS labels 17.5% of deaths outside Census urban areas as urban. Under the fixed Census map, rural deaths went from 18,325 in 2015 to 18,760 in 2024; under the FARS label they went from 17,715 to 16,005."
}